Id: inet007w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_inetd
Fix: Set disable = yes for echo, chargen, daytime, discard and time in /etc/xinetd.d, or comment them out of /etc/inetd.conf.
References: xinetd.conf(5); inetd.conf(5); RFC 862 (Echo), RFC 864 (Character Generator); CERT advisory CA-1996-01 (UDP port denial-of-service)
Controls: CIS 4.8; NIST CM-7, SC-5; ISO 8.21; CE Secure configuration

An enabled super-server (xinetd or inetd) offers one of the small
internal services: echo, chargen, daytime, discard or time. They
serve nothing anyone uses, and because they answer any UDP packet
they reflect traffic to whatever source address a packet claims, and
two of them pointed at each other loop forever: the oldest
denial-of-service amplifier there is. Every distribution ships them
disabled; one that is on was turned on by hand.

Set 'disable = yes' in the service's file under /etc/xinetd.d (or
comment the line out of /etc/inetd.conf) and restart the super-server;
if nothing else is served, remove it.
